Description: Kratheos food data - open food database and its HTTP service
 Serves one food database over HTTP: search as a person types, lookup by
 barcode, read by identifier, and the contributions of users (products
 added, versions of the values and votes, names, reports), from a SQLite
 database rebuilt from open food-composition sources (Open Food Facts, USDA
 FoodData Central, Ciqual, the Swiss Food Composition Database, the Canadian
 Nutrient File, CoFID).
 .
 One process and SQLite only. Reads need no authentication, writes need a
 shared token; the service listens on 127.0.0.1 and is meant to sit behind
 the application that authenticates people.
 .
 Two timers come with it: every week the public layer (kratheos.sqlite) is
 exported from the live database and committed in a clone of the repository;
 every month the main database is rebuilt, checked against the one being
 served, and swapped in without stopping the service.
 .
 The package ships no data. The token and the secret used to hash
 contributor keys are generated on first install in
 /etc/kratheos-food-data/service.conf; data live in
 /var/lib/kratheos-food-data.
